BAGSHAW 11-RANK TABLE TYPO: UNCONDITIONAL HOSTILE -- 2026-08-24
================================================================

STATUS: FINITE-EXACT.  PARI/GP bnfinit discovered the class group and
bnfcertify returned 1, removing the usual GRH condition.

Bagshaw--Jacobson--Scheidler--Rollick Table 5.2 prints

  Delta = -3532321517865683,

while Appendix A.4 prints

  Delta = -3532321517864683.

For the Table 5.2 value, set D=3532321517865683.  Since Delta=-D is odd and
fundamental, its field is generated by a root of

  P=x^2-x+(1+D)/4.

Command in locally extracted PARI/GP 2.13.3:

  default(parisizemax,2000000000); allocatemem(256000000);
  D=3532321517865683;
  P=x^2-x+(1+D)/4;
  B=bnfinit(P,1);
  print("MISPRINT_CYC=",B.cyc,"|H=",B.no);
  print("BNFCERTIFY=",bnfcertify(B));

Output (stack warning omitted):

  MISPRINT_CYC=[3555056, 2, 2]|H=14220224
  BNFCERTIFY=1

Therefore

  Cl(Q(sqrt(-3532321517865683)))
    = Z/3555056 Z + Z/2 Z + Z/2 Z,

and this field has no 11-torsion.  For the Appendix value, the independent
exact positive control is

  11|3|3532321517864683|9266797,1918973,95394449|18021997,-936603,49012309|19135921,-2565769,46233791

Thus the summary-table digit 5 is false and the appendix digit 4 is correct.
